    "name": "Josephson parametric amplifier",
    "category": "amplifier",
    "parent": "stage_mxc",
    "function": "Near-quantum-limited first amplifier: a SQUID-terminated resonator pumped at twice the signal frequency amplifies over a 20 MHz band with about 20 dB gain while adding close to the minimum half photon of noise. It sits at the mixing chamber behind the isolators; its narrow band means it is tuned to one feedline's resonators. Pump leakage back to the qubits must be blocked by the isolators.",
